<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Ha Long by Motorbike: Luggage Packing Guide</h1>
<p>Packing for Ha Long is packing for two climates in one bag, the corridor&rsquo;s long flat hours of sun and wind, and the bay&rsquo;s salty evening, and the machine has to carry both without complaint. This guide packs the trip honestly, the priorities in order, the weight placed where the bike wants it, the rain layer rehearsed, and the dry storage treated as the trip&rsquo;s bank vault, and it refuses to invent weights, volumes or capacities, because the honest answer about what fits is decided by the specific machine at the counter, on your day.</p>
<p>The machine that carries the bag can come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk sees corridor luggage daily and will tell you what their racks and boxes honestly hold. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, study the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/long-distance-motorbike-trip-planning/">long-distance motorbike trip planning</a> guide, see the machines and terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
